H1: the get overlaps the put
  process  operation      called   answered
        1  put x=1            0 ms      10 ms
        2  get x -> 0         5 ms      15 ms
  -> linearizable, e.g. in this order: get->0 put 1

H2: the get starts after the put has finished, but returns the old value
  process  operation      called   answered
        1  put x=1            0 ms      10 ms
        2  get x -> 0        20 ms      30 ms
  -> NOT linearizable

H3: a put never answered; a reader sees 0 after another reader saw 1
  process  operation      called   answered
        1  put x=1            0 ms   no reply
        2  get x -> 1        20 ms      30 ms
        3  get x -> 0        40 ms      50 ms
  -> NOT linearizable

H4: a put never answered; 0 is seen first, then 1
  process  operation      called   answered
        1  put x=1            0 ms   no reply
        2  get x -> 0        20 ms      30 ms
        3  get x -> 1        40 ms      50 ms
  -> linearizable, e.g. in this order: get->0 put 1 get->1

